# Code conventions (Nicolas's style)

- Code lines are preceded by an UPPERCASE `#` comment saying what they do (one comment may cover a short block).
- Every function has a `# FUNCTION: <WHAT IT DOES>` line and a docstring with `Args:` and `Returns:`.
- Suffixes: `_pdf` (DataFrame), `_str`, `_list`, `_dict`, `_arr` (numpy), `_bool`, `_float`, `_int`; parameters end in
  `_in`. Function names say what they return (`get_..._pdf`, `run_..._dict`).
- Module docstrings explain the design in plain words, after the imports.
- Experiment constants live in the experiment's `config.py`; shared constants are read from `so.config`, never copied.
- Timestamps are parsed as UTC and converted to `America/New_York`.
- Files are UTF-8 with LF line endings.
- Tests are plain-assert functions on synthetic data, each ending with `passed("<what was checked>")`.
